      "mimeType": "text",
      "sofaString": "9003\tPt, Naomi Ferraro, is a 16 year old female with a history of autoimmune hepatitis referred for Liver Transplant Psychosocial Assessment.  Information for this assessment was obtained through an interview with the patient and her father, and review of the medical record.  SW spent 45 minutes of face to face time with the family.  Employment: the father was recently laid off from his position at a local warehouse and is currently seeking new employment.  The mother works part time as a home health aide.  Financial situation: the family reports significant financial strain related to the father's recent job loss.  Naomi is currently covered by a combination of private insurance through her mother's employer and state Medicaid.  Transportation: the family's only vehicle is unreliable, which has caused difficulty attending clinic appointments.  Support systems: the family is active in their church community, which provides both emotional and occasional financial support.  There is no smoking or vaping in the home; the father reports quitting smoking two years ago.  Health literacy: the father verbalizes some difficulty understanding the post-transplant medication schedule and would benefit from additional teaching.  Assessment and recommendations: the family is motivated and engaged despite current financial stressors.  Recommendations: connect the family with the hospital's financial counseling office and the transportation assistance program.  Provide additional one-on-one medication education for the father prior to discharge.\n\nOwen Whitfield, LCSW\nPediatric Transplant Team\n(000) 000-0000"
    }
  }
